From 9bbf18baa637ba254ee552c2ed3b9c31a09a2b0d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: stephan-xyz <stephan@zehrer.net>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 09:37:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] rpi-fbd: Raspberry Pi display through the firmware

A display driver for the framebuffer that the Pi firmware scans out. It
asks the firmware, through rpi-firmwared, for a framebuffer of the size a
client sets (the firmware scales it to the monitor mode) and for the
EDID, and registers as a regular display, so fbcond hands the console
over from vesad. It keeps the boot framebuffer while the firmware still
shows it. RPI_FB=WIDTHxHEIGHT makes that size the preferred mode,
RPI_FB=off leaves the display to vesad.
